{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nExactly 63 bloated prose blocks are confirmed in 13 paths under tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/. Condense redundant or historical text while retaining current non-obvious contracts.\n\nInventory and before citations are pinned to origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84. That immutable SHA identifies the audited prose and supplies review citations only. Implement from current origin/main in one commit. Every executable and protected prose comparison uses the committed implementation parent at HEAD^ and the committed final tree at HEAD. Changed path checks use HEAD^..HEAD.\n\n## Boundary and guards\nEdit only the anchored ordinary comments/docstrings below and adjacent blank lines. Currentize RED, pre-fix, “Today”, and implementation-scaffolding prose. Executable statements, assertions, runtime strings, directives, and unlisted prose stay unchanged.\n\nParse committed HEAD^ and HEAD files with ast.parse(source, type_comments=True). Replace only the 54 allowlisted owner docstrings named in Scope with a sentinel. Normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno. Require exact ast.dump(..., include_attributes=False) equality. Every non-allowlisted docstring therefore remains part of the equal AST.\n\nTokenize both committed trees and group comment tokens into contiguous blocks under their innermost qualified AST owner. Resolve the nine allowlisted ordinary comment blocks in HEAD^ by their unique opening phrases from Scope. Record each resolved block as its owner plus its ordinal among that owner's comment blocks. Require the same block count per owner in HEAD. Replace only those nine owner and ordinal positions with a sentinel. Compare every remaining owner, ordinal, column, and comment token byte for equality. This permits line count changes inside an allowlisted block without precomputing final line numbers. It fails if an allowlisted block disappears, splits, or consumes neighboring prose. Compare directive token text and executable attachment separately.\n\n## Scope — 63 editable blocks\n- test_config_jira_wiring.py (4) — module and test_{non_https_jira_url_fails_loud_not_env_fallback,dc_resolver_also_fails_loud_on_non_https_jira_url,bootstrap_env_check_requires_resolved_url_user_token}. Preserve typed-config consumption, HTTPS fail-closed behavior, and bootstrap parity.\n- test_config.py (6) — module; test_{jira_to_local_status_canonical_preimages,jira_to_local_status_round_trips_through_forward_map,jira_to_local_status_parity_with_inbound_differ,local_to_jira_status_parity_with_the_jira_family_map}; comment beginning “Loaded BY PATH”. Replace pre-fix history with current canonical-map parity and import-boundary rationale.\n- test_corrupt_state_guard.py (9) — module; TestBindingStoreCorrupt.{test_corrupt_json_raises_with_named_file,test_git_conflict_markers_in_bindings_raises,test_corrupt_bindings_no_empty_fallback}; TestPrevSnapshotCorrupt plus its test_{prev_snapshot_json_parse_error_helper,corrupt_prev_snapshot_must_not_emit_comment_adds}; TestHealthyStateRegression.test_healthy_snapshot_deduplicates_comments; comment beginning “Defense-in-depth”. Preserve fail-closed state handling and no blind comment emission.\n- test_errors.py (2) — comment beginning “The 9 canonical applier leaf names” and test_authorized_writers_docstring_documents_full_contract. Its concise module docstring is excluded.\n- test_peer_state.py (1) — module. Preserve standalone peer-state round-trip/default behavior.\n- test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py (1) — module. Preserve by-file loading, locked git commit behavior, and non-repository degradation.\n- test_ref_lock_push_classification.py (9) — module; comments beginning “Bug ebee” and “The split of the push/CAS cluster”; test_{non_cas_rejections_are_not_reported_as_a_stolen_lease,cas_mismatch_logs_the_stderr_that_justified_it,a_github_server_side_ref_failure_is_not_reported_as_a_stolen_lease,the_git_patch_point_survives_the_module_split,the_cas_verdict_still_logs_on_the_ref_lock_logger,moved_names_stay_resolvable_at_the_original_module_path}. Preserve lease re-observation, evidence logging, patch points, logger identity, and compatibility exports.\n- test_ref_lock.py (2) — module and _bare_git. Preserve bare-ref CAS behavior and explicit git-dir isolation.\n- test_rich_reemit_state.py (18) — module; test_{rich_sha_takes_cloud_adf_dicts_and_ignores_key_order,an_entry_mutation_survives_the_store_save_reload_round_trip,the_core_flag_read_agrees_with_the_codecs,the_observation_reaches_the_baseline_through_advance_baselines,narrow_operation_persists_the_same_bytes_as_the_legacy_sequence,a_missing_binding_is_nonfatal_and_distinguishable,the_operation_performs_no_save_at_either_layer,the_production_push_never_reaches_a_binding_through_all_bindings,the_production_push_records_through_the_narrow_operation,a_missing_binding_still_skips_the_read_back_after_the_cutover,the_call_site_makes_no_false_claim_about_the_facade,no_production_module_outside_the_read_allowlist_calls_all_bindings}; _AllBindingsWatcher; _production_all_bindings_callers; comments beginning “RP-02 S2 T3”, “9. RP-02 S3 T3”, and “Production modules permitted”. Preserve digest/counter equivalence, sole-writer/no-save boundaries, missing-binding sentinel, and AST caller census.\n- test_richtext_port_heldout.py (2) — module and test_fit_comment_truncates_over_limit_byte_identical. Preserve send-path truncation and neutrality.\n- test_richtext_port.py (1) — module. Preserve neutral-core rich-text/limit port wiring.\n- test_run_differs_wires_refresh_scoped_snapshot_79a4.py (4) — module, _empty_ctx, test_run_differs_invokes_refresh_scoped_snapshot_once_with_ctx, test_refresh_scoped_snapshot_runs_before_the_snapshot_differ. Preserve once-only call and pre-differ ordering.\n- test_scoped_snapshot_overlay_f449.py (4) — module, test_overlay_preserves_snapshot_enrichment_keys, test_stale_snapshot_would_clobber_without_the_overlay, comment beginning “6. the ORCHESTRATOR refresh_scoped_snapshot”. Preserve enrichment merge, stale-snapshot contrast, and wrapper guards.\n\n## Consumers and directives\nPytest collects every module; check_comment_hygiene.py consumes repository prose. test_errors.py inspects production applier/rebar-id authorization documentation: only its own test prose is editable, while executable assertions and production docstrings remain exact. No targeted consumer of an editable docstring was found.\n\nPreserve exactly 26 directive tokens and attachments: config (4 union-attr); corrupt-state (union-attr plus complete E501 and BLE001 noqa tokens); errors (1 union-attr); ref-lock classification (complete BLE001 noqa); ref-lock (1 union-attr); rich-reemit (one import-bootstrap pragma and nine E402 noqas); run-differs (one pragma, one union-attr); scoped-overlay (two pragmas and two E402 noqas).\n\n## Independent receipt\nA non-author reviewer posts exactly 63 leaf-linked TSV rows:\npath<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session\n\nCitations use full SHAs, every after count is lower, and both verdicts are PASS. Missing, duplicate, or extra rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 63 allowlisted prose blocks change.\n- [ ] Exactly 54 allowlisted owner docstrings change.\n- [ ] Exactly nine allowlisted ordinary comment blocks change.\n- [ ] Every changed block has a lower final word count.\n- [ ] Every changed block states current rationale or constraints.\n- [ ] Every non-allowlisted docstring remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every non-allowlisted ordinary comment token remains byte-identical at the same owner, ordinal, and column.\n- [ ] All 26 directive tokens retain exact text and executable attachment.\n- [ ] The committed HEAD^ and HEAD normalized AST comparison exits 0.\n- [ ] The committed HEAD^ and HEAD ordinary comment comparison exits 0.\n- [ ] The changed path command reports exactly the 13 file impact paths.\n- [ ] The diff integrity command exits 0.\n- [ ] The comment hygiene command exits 0.\n- [ ] The focused 13-module test command exits 0.\n- [ ] Worktree virtualenv make lint exits 0 before push.\n- [ ] Worktree virtualenv make typecheck exits 0 before push.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV contains exactly 63 complete rows.\n- [ ] Every TSV stable ID is unique.\n- [ ] Every TSV row cites the full immutable before SHA.\n- [ ] Every TSV row cites the full final SHA.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records semantic-preservation as PASS.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records bloat-removal as PASS.\n- [ ] Every TSV row names a non-author reviewer session.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review is +1 before merge.\n- [ ] Gerrit Verified is +1 before merge.\n\n## Verification\nRun all six structured commands. Do not run the full local suite for this comments and documentation leaf. Gerrit CI provides repository-wide verification."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788983461578375001,"uuid":"d0f8eeb8-0da0-419e-8c89-c5ce96d8e4e4"}